          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The special case where the class of the restriction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            to the D-brane
            %em equals
            the third
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+Stiefel-Whitney+class"} integral Stiefel-Whitney class
            of the D-brane was discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              %em Anomalies in String Theory with D-Branes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9907189"}> arXiv:hep-th/9907189
              )
          %p
            The generalization to the case that the two classes differ by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
            class was considered in
          %ul
            %li#Kapustin99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-branes in a topologically nontrivial B-field
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909089"} arXiv:hep-th/9909089
          %p
            Aspects of the interpretation of this by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} push-forward in generalized cohomology
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            are formalized in
          %ul#CareyWang05
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"}> Alan Carey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bai-Ling+Wang"} Bai-Ling Wang
              %em Thom isomorphism and Push-forward map in twisted K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0507414"}> arXiv:math/0507414
              )
          %p and section 10 of
          %ul#AndoBlumbergGepner10
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twists of K-theory and TMF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=PSPUM-81"} vol 81
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3004"} arXiv:1002.3004
          %p
            (which discusses twists as
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-module+bundles"} (infinity,1)-module bundles
          %p
            The formulation by postcomposition with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphisms"} dual morphisms
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            which we use above is based on the observations in section 7 of
          %ul#BrodzkiMathaiRosenbergSzabo06
            %li
              Jacek Brodzki,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-Branes, RR-Fields and Duality on Noncommutative Manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607020"} arXiv:hep-th/0607020
          %p
            and generalized to equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            in
          %ul#Tu06
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Tu"}> Jean-Louis Tu
              ,
              %em Twisted K-theory and Poincaré duality
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609556"}> arXiv:math/0609556
              )
          %p A clean formulation and review is provided in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Loriano Bonora, Fabio Ferrari Ruffino, Raffaele Savelli,
                %em Classifying A-field and B-field configurations in the presence of D-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4291"}> arXiv:0810.4291
                )
            %li
              %p
                Fabio Ferrari Ruffino,
                %em Topics on topology and superstring theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4524"}> arXiv:0910.4524
                )
            %li
              %p
                Fabio Ferrari Ruffino,
                %em Classifying A-field and B-field configurations in the presence of D-branes - Part II: Stacks of D-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.2798"}> arXiv:1104.2798
                )
            %li
              %p
                Raffaele Savelli,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Freed-Witten Anomaly and Charge/Flux quantization in String/F Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://digitallibrary.sissa.it/bitstream/handle/1963/4999/PhDthesisSavelli.pdf?sequence=1"} pdf
          %p and
          %ul#Laine
            %li
              Kim Laine,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric and topological aspects of Type IIB D-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0460"} arXiv:0912.0460
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Laine"}> Laine
            ) the discussion of FW-anomaly cancellation with finite-rank gauge bundles is towards the very end, culminating in equation (3.41).
          %p
            A discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            is at the end of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
              \.
          %p
            Lecture notes along these lines are in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#3dCSTheory"} Lagrangians and Action functionals – 3d Chern-Simons theory
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
              \.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-description" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          %ul#Nuiten
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local prequantum boundary field theory
          %h3#relation_to_shifted_cfield_flux Relation to shifted C-field flux
          %p
            On relating the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly"} Freed-Witten anomaly
            to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , Section 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality Relations Among Topological Effects In String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9912086"} arXiv:hep-th/9912086
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
          %ul
